<article class="env-example" id="0GEW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GEW">Example <span data-tag="0GEW">48.3.9</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism of Noetherian schemes, $L \in D^-_{\textit{Coh}}(X)$ and $K \in D^+_{\mathit{QCoh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$. Then the map $Rf_*R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(L, a(K)) \to R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ Y}(Rf_*L, K)$ is an isomorphism. Namely, the complexes $L$ and $Rf_*L$ are pseudo-coherent by Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/08E8" data-tag="08E8">36.10.3</a> and <a href="/tag/08E2" data-tag="08E2">36.11.3</a> and the discussion in Remark <a href="/tag/0GEV" data-tag="0GEV">48.3.8</a> applies. </p>
</article>